# Re-pricing the 2026-09-16 activation-object sizing against the MEASURED dispatch floor
UTC:      2026-09-20 (Desktop 2, DESKTOP-CBL5NUA)
COMMIT:   ignite-xdna Canary 88c4605 (detached worktree split-audit)
INPUTS:   MEASURED - results/aie/split_segment_floor_phoenix_20260920.log (this session's NOP sitting,
          six models, 300/200 dispatches each, xrt-smi idle before every container)
          MEASURED - 6.898931 GB/s per column achievable DDR passthrough (the four-lever silicon sitting)
          QUOTED   - results/aie/notes_yolov8s_gap.md:384-392, the sweep's own cost model and results
STATUS:   DERIVED re-pricing over measured inputs. No container was built at any other object size and
          nothing here has been run on silicon. It changes a cost model, not a measurement.

WHY: the 541-candidate sweep that kept A_BYTES at 6,400 is NOT in the repo - only its results are. Its
cost model, however, is stated in the notes, and that is reproducible. The sweep's TOTAL was right to
1.1% against the floor measured three days later, but its SPLIT was not, and the split is what scores
a candidate.
