STEP 2 - what the sweep assumed, from its own words (notes_yolov8s_gap.md:384-392)
  yolov8s: 224.6 MB at 26.8 GB/s = 8.38 ms transport, 'roughly 5.1 ms of issue for 8772 merged quad tasks'
  => 0.581 us per task, and a split of 62.2% transport / 37.8% issue.
  Its TOTAL is right: 13.48 ms against the 13.340 ms measured floor (1.1%).

STEP 3 - the error: it priced CORE-SIDE bytes at the DDR rate
  Only shim-side bytes cross DDR. yolov8s moves 74,511,488 B over the shim, not 224.6 MB:
  the MemTile re-serves overlapping windows to the four cores, so core-side traffic is 3.01x the wire.
  measured  transport 2.700 ms (20.2%) | per-task 10.640 ms (79.8%)
  sweep     transport 8.381 ms (62.2%) | issue    5.100 ms (37.8%)
  => the sweep over-counted transport 3.10x and under-counted per-task cost 2.56x
     (2.09x if you normalise its issue cost onto the same 7143 shim tasks)

